{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'rg -n -A55 -B8 \"Dissent block|type: dissent|## Dissent|severity:|requested resolution\" coord/AGENTS_PROTOCOL.md'","aggregated_output":"340-[blocker|suggestion|nit][correctness|coordination|security|operability|test-gap|scope|docs|cost] finding text\n341-```\n342-\n343-Severity keeps its existing meaning. Category records the risk:\n344-`correctness`, `coordination`, `security`, `operability`, `test-gap`, `scope`,\n345-`docs`, or `cost`.\n346-\n347-Dissent is a structured objection to a decision, route, synthesis, rejection,\n348:or risk acceptance. Use `type: dissent` with a `Dissent:` body containing\n349-`severity`, `category`, `against`, `claim`, `evidence`,\n350:`requested resolution`, and `proposed next step`. A blocker dissent blocks\n351-clean task close until the lead posts a resolving `type: decision` with\n352-`Resolves: <dissent-rev-or-op-id>` and one result: `accepted`,\n353-`rejected-because`, `deferred`, or `escalated`. Request/result mapping is:\n354-`accept` -> `accepted`, `reject-with-rationale` -> `rejected-because`, and\n355-`escalate-to-principal` or `open-council` -> `escalated`. `deferred` is a\n356-lead-initiated result that must name the follow-up owner and condition. If\n357-rejection does not converge, escalate to `coord/HUMAN.md` or open a council\n358-route.\n359-\n360-Council-as-route reuses `coord-council.sh`: sealed proposals, anonymized\n361-ranking, Borda tally, and chair synthesis. The chair posts a `type: decision`\n362-linking the `coord/council/C-NNN.../decision.md`; after that, implementation\n363-returns to targeted or full-mesh review according to importance. A task on\n364-`Review route: council` cannot close cleanly unless `Council session: C-NNN`\n365-points at a real decided session under `coord/council/`.\n366-\n367-## Disagreement\n368-\n369-Critique code, scope, assumptions, or risk; never the person. A disagreement\n370-must include both the reason and a concrete alternative.\n371-\n372-If two rounds do not converge, stop debating and add the decision to\n373-`coord/HUMAN.md`.\n374-\n375-## Heartbeats\n376-\n377-When agents are actively coordinating and waiting on each other, they should\n378-check or append at the agreed cadence. Automation is optional. The protocol must\n379-still work when agents only wake on user invocation.\n380-\n381-### Iteration Mode\n382-\n383-Iteration mode is an optional operating mode for unattended or lightly\n384-supervised collaboration.\n385-\n386-Required fields live in `coord/OPERATING_MODE.md`:\n387-\n388-- active task;\n389-- lead and reviewer;\n390-- active thread;\n391-- check cadence;\n392-- next check due;\n393-- stop condition;\n394-- edit budget;\n395-- wake targets for agents that an external wrapper should be able to wake;\n396-- file ownership.\n397-- active loop drivers, if any, with agent, mechanism, cadence, started_at,\n398-  stop_condition, persistence, and last_seen_thread_rev.\n399-\n400-Use `type: iteration-start` when entering iteration mode, `type:\n401-iteration-check` for periodic updates, and `type: iteration-stop` when the stop\n402-condition is met. Closed threads stay in `coord/threads/`; `coord/STATE.md` stops pointing to them. Add a final `type: handoff`, `type: decision`, or `type: iteration-stop` message summarizing the resolution.\n403-\n404-Before `iteration-stop`, verify: canonical source is clean if touched; local\n405-provenance is updated; no pending `ack: false` message is directed at the lead;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
